text:
anya: quick accessibility review of the datasets table sort controls (table header buttons). Found a couple of issues: no aria-sort updates, sort icons are purely decorative (no text alternative), and keyboard focus on sort button is very subtle (hard to see).

rachel: thanks — which AT/browser did you test with?

anya: tested in Firefox+NVDA and Safari+VoiceOver. Steps: focus header by tabbing to column name -> press Enter to toggle sort. NVDA doesn't read the new sort state; VoiceOver announces the button but not whether it's ascending/descending. Also the visual chevron is 8px and color contrast against header bg is low.

a11y-bot: Automated checks: header button color #6b7280 vs bg #ffffff => contrast 3.2:1 (WARNING for UI icons). aria-sort attribute missing on TH elements. role=\"button\" applied to non-button element (FAIL semantic).

tanner: oof — we rendered headers as <div role=\"button\"> for style reasons. We can swap to native <button> inside TH or add aria-pressed/aria-sort. Thoughts?

joel: prefer native semantics. Use <button> and visually hide default focus until focus-visible. Also make sure aria-sort is present on the TH or button depending on pattern. For table sorting, using aria-sort on TH is recommended: aria-sort=\"none|ascending|descending|other\".

mike: UX question: we also have an indicator that shows sorted column with a filled chevron. Need accessible label that conveys \"Sorted ascending\" or \"Sorted descending\".

anya: suggested fixes: 1) swap to <th><button aria-label=\"Sort by Name, currently unsorted\">Name <span class=\"visually-hidden\">(sorted ascending)</span></button></th> and update the visually-hidden text on toggle 2) add aria-sort on <th> instead of role button 3) bump chevron color to meet 4.5:1 for important controls 4) ensure focus-visible style is strong and not removed.

rachel: can you paste minimal markup + CSS + small JS for aria updates so I can drop into the component?

anya: yup, quick example:

```html
<!-- markup idea -->
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th aria-sort=\"none\">
        <button class=\"th-sort\">Name <span class=\"chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\">▾</span><span class=\"sr-only\">Sorted: none</span></button>
      </th>
      <!-- other headers -->
    </tr>
  </thead>
</table>
```

```css
/* styles */
.th-sort { background: none; border: none; padding: 8px; font: inherit; color: #111827; }
.th-sort:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #2563eb; outline-offset: 2px; border-radius: 4px; }
.chevron { color: #0f172a; /* higher contrast */ font-size: 12px; }
.sr-only { position: absolute !important; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0,0,0,0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }
```

```js
// JS to toggle aria-sort and SR text
const headers = document.querySelectorAll('th[aria-sort]');
headers.forEach(th => {
  const btn = th.querySelector('button');
  btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const current = th.getAttribute('aria-sort');
    const next = current === 'ascending' ? 'descending' : 'ascending';
    // reset others
    headers.forEach(h => h.setAttribute('aria-sort', 'none'));
    th.setAttribute('aria-sort', next);
    // update sr-only text
    const sr = btn.querySelector('.sr-only');
    sr.textContent = `Sorted: ${next}`;
    // update aria-label for extra clarity
    btn.setAttribute('aria-label', `Sort by ${btn.textContent.trim().replace(/Sorted:.*$/,'')}, currently ${next}`);
  });
});
```

tanner: LGTM — small tweak: avoid putting the SR label inside the button textContent change logic; use data attributes to build aria-label so we don't include SR text twice for ATs. Also ensure the chevron has aria-hidden and status is only via aria-sort.

anya: good call. Also add keyboard support for Space and Enter; native button already handles that. If we ever used role=\"button\" we'd need keydown handlers.

ajoel: test suggestions: run axe-core to verify no duplicate role errors, check NVDA reads aria-sort on header and NVDA reports when it changes. Add an Acceptance test to tab through headers and assert focus-visible present.

a11y-bot: queued checks: aria-sort presence, button semantics, focus-visible rules, icon contrast.

mike: one more UI affordance: when a table has many columns, keyboard users might lose context. Consider an offscreen live region that announces \"Table sorted by NAME, ascending\" on change. Use role=\"status\" and aria-live=\"polite\" on the live region.

rachel: good idea. Keep the live region separate, only update its text on sort change. Don't update aria-live too frequently.

anya: final PR notes I'll include: \"Convert header sort controls to native buttons, add aria-sort to TH, provide sr-only status text and optional polite live region for screen reader announcements, improve chevron contrast, and ensure clear focus-visible outlines.\" I'll attach snippets and axe results.

mike: thanks! assigning @tanner to implement and @rachel to review.

rachel: will add unit + e2e checks for aria-sort and focus style.

anya: thanks all — filing PR now. :shipit:
